export const knowledgeDocuments = [{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Product map, account, and privacy","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Product map, account, and privacy","content":"# Product map, account, and privacy\n\nProgressTracker stores personal activities as trackers and dated check-ins. It works locally first; signing in enables account synchronization. AI Help explains product behavior but has no permission to query personal trackers or make changes."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Where features live","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Where features live","content":"## Where features live\n\n| Feature | Location | Main purpose |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Today | `/` | See today’s tracker opportunities and record check-ins. |\n| Trackers | `/trackers` | Create, edit, pause, archive, restore, and organize tracker definitions. |\n| Goals | `/goals` | Review saved goal plans, pacing, and milestones. |\n| Calendar | `/calendar` | Review activity by date and navigate the calendar. |\n| History | `/history` | Inspect past check-ins and their saved values. |\n| Insights / Analytics | `/dashboard`, `/analytics` | Review progress summaries and per-measure observations. |\n| Holidays & breaks | `/holidays` | Manage date-specific breaks that affect scheduled opportunities. |\n| Settings | `/settings` | Change profile, sync, time-zone, appearance, notification, and account settings. |\n\nThe visible navigation groups some routes: Calendar includes History, and Insights includes Analytics, Achievements, and the dashboard. Route availability depends on account state for account-specific settings."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Create a tracker","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Create a tracker","content":"## Create a tracker\n\n1. Open **Trackers** and choose **Create tracker** (or use the creation link from an empty Today view).\n2. Choose Habit or Goal. Open **Challenge or project?** for those tracker kinds.\n3. Enter a name, then choose the measure type and configure its values. New measures use Yes/No or Quantity.\n4. Set the schedule, active dates, and any strict-mode behavior that fits the tracker.\n5. Expand advanced settings to configure success rules, custom check-in fields, milestones, or goal planning when needed.\n6. Save. The tracker is saved locally on this device; signed-in accounts synchronize it when online.\n\nThe setup page remains a single form. A validation error identifies the relevant field or section; correct it and submit again. If leaving a modified form, keep editing or explicitly discard the changes."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Edit a tracker","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Edit a tracker","content":"## Edit a tracker\n\nOpen the tracker from **Trackers**, then choose its edit action. You can update supported settings and add new measures. A saved measure’s type and historical interpretation are protected. Retire a measure with history to remove it from future check-ins while retaining the definition for old entries. Resolve rule, milestone, or plan dependencies before removing or retiring a measure.\n\nArchiving or pausing a tracker changes whether it is active for future opportunities; it does not erase recorded history. Deleting to the Bin is a separate lifecycle action and follows the app’s restore/permanent-delete flow."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Check-ins and custom fields","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Check-ins and custom fields","content":"## Check-ins and custom fields\n\nA check-in records the values for active measures on a date. Custom check-in fields, such as a short note or selected answer, add context to that entry; they are not measure values and are not used as numeric goal totals. A deliberate skip is different from recording a value. Editing the same date keeps the latest live revision for current calculations; deleted/tombstoned entries are excluded from current progress."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Account, local data, and synchronization","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Account, local data, and synchronization","content":"## Account, local data, and synchronization\n\nLocal tracker definitions, entries, and workspace preferences use browser storage. Signing in enables Supabase synchronization for account-owned records. When offline, local work remains on the device and sync can resume later. The sync engine uses revisions and records conflicts instead of silently combining incompatible tracker edits. Resolve a conflict from the app’s sync/conflict flow; do not assume both versions were merged.\n\nWorkspace time zone and appearance are saved locally for that workspace and currently do not synchronize across devices. A time-zone change changes date interpretation going forward; date-only check-in records are not shifted to a different date.\n\nAccount settings include profile-name edits, email-change confirmation, password controls in Sync & Data, notifications, account deletion, and workspace preferences. The app uses Supabase Auth for sign-in and profile/account operations. A user must confirm an email change through the sent verification message.\n\n### Create an account and sign in\n\nOpen the account screen from **Settings** or the sign-in prompt. **Email me a sign-in link** sends a one-time email link; using an email for the first time creates an account, while using an existing account’s email signs that account in. To create an account with a password, choose **Create account**, enter an email and a password of at least eight characters, and submit. Existing password users can choose **Use password** and sign in with their email and password. A magic link is an alternative sign-in method and does not require setting a password.\n\nSigned-in users can choose **Set or change password** under **Settings → Sync & Data** and save a new password of at least eight characters. **Forgot password?** sends an account recovery link; open it to choose a new password. Recovery and email confirmation continue to use Supabase’s email links. Depending on the project’s Secure email change setting, an email change may require links from both the current and new inboxes; until every required confirmation is completed, the current address remains active.\n\n### Delete your account\n\nAccount deletion is available in the app for signed-in users under **Settings → Account Actions → Delete Account**. Review the permanent-deletion notice, enter the account password and the exact word `DELETE`, then choose **Permanently Delete Account**. Password verification is checked by the server and authorizes one deletion for up to five minutes. If you normally use email sign-in links, set a password first under **Settings → Sync & Data → Set or change password**. If the app says it could not reach the deletion service, keep the confirmation open and retry the deletion status when online; the server checks whether deletion already completed before trying again.\n\nThe app reports pending offline changes before the final confirmation; those changes are not uploaded as part of deletion. Export the workspace first if you want a copy. The server removes the Supabase Auth account and its account-owned cloud records. This device switches to guest mode and clears the deleted account's local workspace only after the server confirms deletion. Other devices can retain local copies and must be cleared separately. If the server cannot confirm the result, the app keeps local data and may pause synchronization until the deletion status is checked.\n\nIf deletion fails, read the message shown in the confirmation dialog and retry only after resolving its cause. For help, contact **spraha.progresstracker@gmail.com**. P"},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Calendar, holidays, Insights, and achievements","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Calendar, holidays, Insights, and achievements","content":"## Calendar, holidays, Insights, and achievements\n\nThe **Calendar** page shows activity by date. Use it to review where activity was recorded or an opportunity was missed; History provides the detailed saved values. The **Holidays & breaks** page manages date-only account holidays used by schedule-aware views. In Standard Mode, a holiday removes that date from expected opportunities; Strict Mode still requires activity on an active calendar day.\n\nThe **Insights** overview combines recent counts and consistency across active trackers, while keeping each tracker’s streak separate. Its activity heatmap shows daily completion relative to that date’s eligible opportunities; on narrow screens its automatic default shows a shorter range, and the user can select a period/year. The range choice is stored for the browser session. The legacy **Achievements** view summarizes saved-history points and streaks. When the progression view is enabled for a build, **Wins** shows confirmed XP and 14 server-authoritative badges, including repeatable Perfect Month and The Comeback awards. Reconstructed XP does not unlock badges, and offline estimates remain provisional until the server confirms them. These progression rewards do not change tracker records or goals. When viewing all trackers, points and counts may be added, but different tracker streak lengths are not combined."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Notifications and the Bin","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Notifications and the Bin","content":"## Notifications and the Bin\n\nSigned-in users can configure reminders under **Settings → Notifications**: reminders for today’s unmarked activities, unresolved activity from yesterday, optional partially completed targets, motivational messages, quiet hours, and daily caps. Reminder times use the workspace time zone and foreground checks run while the app is open. Device permission and push subscription registration do not mean closed-app delivery is available; the app explicitly reports that background sender/scheduler setup is not deployed. Guests do not have account notification preferences.\n\nDeleted trackers appear on the separate **The Bin** page at **More → Bin** for a 30-day recovery period. The Bin shows **Restore**, which brings back the tracker and its saved progress/planning data, and **Permanently delete**, which permanently removes the tracker and its associated history after server confirmation. Production shows the permanent-delete action when the `VITE_ENABLE_PERMANENT_DELETION` build-time flag is `true`. The hosted manual deletion RPC and its permissions have been verified. Automatic cleanup is not configured because `pg_cron` is not installed; users should not expect trackers to be removed automatically after 30 days. Archiving, deleting into the Bin, restoring, and permanently deleting are different actions."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Feedback and Support","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Feedback and Support","content":"## Feedback and Support\n\nSigned-in users can send a support query, bug report, feature request, or general feedback from **Settings → Feedback & Support** or the AI Help panel. In-app submissions are saved to the account’s support history and routed to ProgressTracker support. Users can review replies and respond under **Settings → My Support Queries**; resolved conversations are read-only, so a new query is needed to continue. Maintainer replies appear in the existing notification center and open the linked conversation. **Email Support** opens an external mail app and is not stored in the in-app support history. Account deletion removes that account’s feedback, support messages, notifications, and pending email jobs. AI Help sends only the text explicitly submitted in the support form, not the surrounding chat."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: Local backup","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"Local backup","content":"## Local backup\n\nIn **Settings → Sync & Data**, the local backup controls can download a workspace backup and restore a JSON backup into the same guest workspace or account. Restore previews additions and conflicts, adds missing records, skips identical records, and stops without changing data if IDs or dates conflict. A backup is a portability/recovery file; it is not proof that cloud synchronization succeeded. Keep it in a safe place because it can contain workspace records."},{"slug":"core-application","title":"ProgressTracker product map: AI Help privacy and availability","path":"docs/ai-help/core-application.md","section":"AI Help privacy and availability","content":"## AI Help privacy and availability\n\nThe browser sends the question, a bounded set of recent chat messages, and a fixed route identifier. It does not attach tracker definitions, check-in values, journals, goals, profile fields, or workspace preferences. The assistant cannot inspect a user’s personal records, edit the workspace, or execute actions.\n\nRemote answers require an authenticated session and connectivity. A small local FAQ can answer selected common questions while signed out or offline; it cannot search the full product knowledge bundle. Provider, configuration, and rate-limit failures are shown with a recoverable message. Retry after any displayed cooldown.\n\nSource references: `src/routes/router.tsx`, `src/app/AppShell.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx`, `src/domain/trackers/schemaVersionGate.ts`, `supabase/migrations/20261010000100_tracker_bin_permanent_deletion.sql`, `src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx`, `src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx`, `src/features/dashboard/AchievementsPage.tsx`, `src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx`, `src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx`, `src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx`, `src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx`, `src/features/auth/authService.ts`, `src/features/auth/WorkspaceBackup.tsx`, `src/features/settings/AccountDeletion.tsx`, `src/config/supportContact.ts`, `src/features/feedback/SendFeedback.tsx`, `src/features/feedback/MySupportQueries.tsx`, `src/features/feedback/supportApi.ts`, `src/features/ai-knowledge/SupportInboxWorkspace.tsx`, `src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx`, `src/components/NotificationCenter.tsx`, `src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx`, `src/features/settings/appearance.ts`, `src/features/ai-help/AIHelpAssistant.tsx`, `src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts`, `src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `src/db/database.ts`, `supabase/migrations/20261030000200_unified_feedback_support.sql`, `supabase/functions/send-feedback/index.ts`, `supabase/functions/support-inbox/index.ts`, `supabase/functions/ai-help-feedback/index.ts`, `supabase/functions/ai-help-review/index.ts`, `supabase/functions/ai-help/index.ts`, `supabase/functions/delete-account/index.ts`."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Measures, check-in values, and success rules","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Measures, check-in values, and success rules","content":"# Measures, check-in values, and success rules\n\nA measure is one named value recorded as part of a tracker check-in. Measures let a tracker record more than a simple completed/not-completed state. They are the values used by thresholds, goal plans, milestones, history, and analytics."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Choose a measure type","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Choose a measure type","content":"## Choose a measure type\n\nNew measures can be **Yes/No** or **Quantity**.\n\n- Choose **Yes/No** for a state with two answers, such as “Did I stretch?” or “Did I take a break?”. A true value can qualify according to the tracker’s rule; false is still a recorded answer, but does not satisfy a true condition.\n- Choose **Quantity** for a nonnegative number, such as pages, minutes, repetitions, or dollars. Add a unit when it clarifies what the number represents. Precision controls the allowed increment and does not silently round saved targets.\n\nEach tracker needs at least one active measure. It can have multiple measures, each with its own stable ID, name, type, unit, precision, and thresholds. For example, a study tracker could record “Minutes” as Quantity and “Reviewed notes” as Yes/No. Units stay independent per measure."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Legacy measure formats","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Legacy measure formats","content":"## Legacy measure formats\n\nSome existing trackers may still contain **Duration** or **Checklist** measures. They remain readable and usable for existing definitions, but new measures cannot select those types.\n\nDuration is a legacy nonnegative numeric value, commonly interpreted with a unit such as minutes. A legacy Checklist has named items with separate checked states. It is not a single Yes/No answer: the check-in retains each checked item, and supported threshold, milestone, and planning calculations use the checked-item count. For a new tracker, use separate Yes/No measures when each named item needs its own state, or Quantity when only a total count matters."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Editing, type immutability, and retirement","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Editing, type immutability, and retirement","content":"## Editing, type immutability, and retirement\n\nAfter a measure is saved, its type cannot be changed. A saved measure with recorded values must retain the name, unit, type, and meaning needed to interpret that history. To track something different, add a new measure and keep the old one for its existing entries.\n\nAn unsaved measure can be removed. A saved measure with no references or history may be removed safely. A measure with history should be **retired**, not deleted: it disappears from future check-in forms while its definition and values remain available in History and Analytics. Retired measures cannot be reactivated. Keep at least one active measure for future check-ins. If rules, milestones, or goal plans refer to the measure, resolve those references before retiring or removing it."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Thresholds versus goal targets","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Thresholds versus goal targets","content":"## Thresholds versus goal targets\n\nQuantity measures can define per-check-in achievement levels:\n\n- **Minimum** is the first threshold that counts as some achievement.\n- **Target** is the intended per-check-in result.\n- **Stretch** is a higher achievement level.\n\nThese thresholds classify a single check-in. A planning target describes progress expected repeatedly or accumulated over a date range; it is configured separately. For example, a per-check-in Target of 20 pages is not automatically the same as a cumulative goal total of 500 pages.\n\nWhen direction is **increase**, a value at or above a level reaches it. When direction is **decrease**, a value at or below the level reaches it. Numeric check-in values and thresholds are nonnegative. A zero increasing threshold can qualify every nonnegative value, so invalid always-qualifying configurations are rejected. Zero may still be meaningful for a decreasing target or as a planning boundary; do not assume every zero means “complete”."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Success rules","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Success rules","content":"## Success rules\n\nA success rule answers: “Does this check-in qualify?” It does not change the stored value. Rules can compare a measure directly or test a configured threshold. Conditions can be combined with:\n\n- **All (AND):** every condition must pass.\n- **Any (OR):** at least one condition must pass.\n- **At least N:** the selected number of child conditions must pass.\n\nThese groups can be nested. Boolean measures can be compared with Yes/No. Numeric and legacy Checklist values can be compared against supported thresholds or numbers. Conditions referencing a retired or removed measure must be resolved before the measure can leave the active configuration. A custom success rule should not be silently reset when a measure is removed.\n\nSuccess qualification feeds streak and completion summaries. A recorded value may therefore appear in History even when it does not qualify for a streak. A scheduled day with no qualifying check-in is not the same as a rest day."},{"slug":"measures-and-success-rules","title":"Measures and success rules: Common choices and troubleshooting","path":"docs/ai-help/measures-and-success-rules.md","section":"Common choices and troubleshooting","content":"## Common choices and troubleshooting\n\n- **“I only need to check whether I did it.”** Use Yes/No.\n- **“I need to record how much.”** Use Quantity with a suitable unit and precision.\n- **“Why can’t I convert an old measure?”** Its existing values were recorded using the saved type. Add a new measure for a different interpretation; retire the old one if it should no longer appear in new check-ins.\n- **“Why is a check-in not counting toward my streak?”** Check the tracker’s success rule, the value recorded, whether the date is scheduled, the tracker’s active dates, and whether a holiday or strict mode changes the opportunity.\n- **“Why can’t I retire this measure?”** Look for rule, milestone, or planning references, and confirm another active measure will remain.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/types.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/schema.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/invariants.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/progression.ts`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/trackerSetupSchema.ts`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.test.tsx`, `src/domain/trackers/schema.test.ts`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `supabase/migrations/20261018000100_tracker_metric_integrity.sql`."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: Schedules, activity status, and streaks","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"Schedules, activity status, and streaks","content":"# Schedules, activity status, and streaks\n\nA schedule defines when a tracker is expected to have an opportunity. It affects Today, activity status, streaks, plan pacing, and Analytics consistency; it does not create or delete check-ins."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: Schedule options","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"Schedule options","content":"## Schedule options\n\nThe tracker setup form offers common schedules such as every day, weekdays, and three times a week. Existing or advanced tracker definitions can also use selected weekdays, every N days, a chosen number of occurrences per week or month, specific dates, a one-time date, or no scheduled occurrences. A custom schedule is preserved when editing rather than silently replaced by a simpler option.\n\nThe effective start date is the later of the configured start and the tracker’s creation date interpreted in the workspace time zone. A deadline bounds the active period. An occurrence outside that interval is not a scheduled opportunity."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: Standard Mode and Strict Mode","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"Standard Mode and Strict Mode","content":"## Standard Mode and Strict Mode\n\nIn **Standard Mode**, only scheduled dates that are not holidays count as expected opportunities. Unscheduled rest days and holidays do not break a streak or lower consistency. In **Strict Mode**, each active calendar day is treated as an opportunity, including rest days and past holidays; a qualifying entry is required to preserve the streak.\n\nChanging modes recalculates the tracker’s streak interpretation but does not delete recorded progress. Standard Mode is often appropriate for routines with planned rest days. Strict Mode is appropriate only when every active day should require a qualifying check-in."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: What counts as a streak day","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"What counts as a streak day","content":"## What counts as a streak day\n\nA check-in must be recorded and meet the tracker’s success rule to qualify. For a Yes/No measure, the rule can require true. Quantity and legacy measures can use a configured qualification level or their supported recorded-value behavior. A value may be saved and visible in History even if it does not qualify for the streak.\n\nA required day in the past without a qualifying entry breaks the current run. In Standard Mode, an unscheduled rest day and a holiday are neutral. A deliberately skipped required opportunity fails for streak and Perfect Day purposes, but it is not treated as a completed check-in. The current date remains pending while an outcome is unresolved; a known failure can make the day fail before it closes. Dates after the as-of date are future, not missed.\n\nThe tracker deadline limits opportunities. A paused, archived, or deleted tracker does not create new active opportunities, while its recorded history remains viewable. The longest streak is historical; the current streak reflects the present run through the as-of date. Each tracker has its own streak. The separate All Trackers streak counts consecutive dates when every required tracker qualifies; it is not the sum of individual streaks. A date with no required tracker is neutral, and pending dates do not prematurely break a confirmed run.\n\nA Perfect Day requires at least one required tracker and qualifying completion for every required tracker. Perfect Week is repeatable for each completed Monday-based calendar week with all required opportunities qualifying and at least three required activity dates. Perfect Month is repeatable for each completed calendar month with all required opportunities qualifying and at least twelve required activity dates. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral for those periods; Strict Mode dates remain required. Consistency Star uses the average of daily adherence across the latest 30 completed eligible dates, where each day is qualifying eligible trackers divided by eligible trackers. These period badges and consistency use different thresholds and are not interchangeable."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: Holidays and breaks","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"Holidays and breaks","content":"## Holidays and breaks\n\nHolidays are date-only workspace records. In Standard Mode they remove that date from expected scheduled opportunities. In Strict Mode, an active past holiday remains a required calendar day for streak qualification. Holidays affect pacing and consistency calculations as well as streak continuity. They do not erase an entry stored on that date."},{"slug":"schedules-and-streaks","title":"Schedules and streaks: Troubleshooting examples","path":"docs/ai-help/schedules-and-streaks.md","section":"Troubleshooting examples","content":"## Troubleshooting examples\n\n- **A Sunday did not break my streak:** confirm Sunday is not scheduled and the tracker uses Standard Mode.\n- **A rest day did break my streak:** Strict Mode treats active calendar days as opportunities; switch modes only if that matches the intended rule.\n- **A recorded day did not extend the streak:** inspect the success rule and the values in that check-in; a recorded entry can be partial.\n- **Today appears pending:** that is expected until today’s check-in is submitted. Past unfilled scheduled dates can become missed.\n- **A schedule edit changed the consistency percentage:** the denominator is the set of opportunities under the current schedule and mode; saved check-ins remain intact.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/planning.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/progression.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.test.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts`, `src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx`, `src/features/today/TodayPage.test.tsx`, `src/domain/holidays.ts`, `src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx`."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Goals, planning, and milestones","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Goals, planning, and milestones","content":"# Goals, planning, and milestones\n\nUse planning targets to describe progress over time. They are separate from a measure’s per-check-in Minimum, Target, and Stretch thresholds. Planning belongs to the tracker and keeps each measure’s unit and target separate."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Find and configure a goal plan","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Find and configure a goal plan","content":"## Find and configure a goal plan\n\nCreate or edit a tracker in **Trackers**. In its setup form, open **Planning targets** under the advanced settings, choose a planning mode, then enter targets for the eligible measures. The **Goals** page shows saved plans and their progress. The setup form preserves both daily and cumulative target maps when switching modes; changing the mode does not delete check-ins."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Daily recurring plan","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Daily recurring plan","content":"## Daily recurring plan\n\nA daily recurring plan sets a target for each scheduled opportunity. For example, “read 10 pages on each scheduled weekday” is checked one day at a time. Its consistency percentage is the number of met opportunities divided by elapsed opportunities. Rest days and holidays are neutral, and an unsubmitted current day stays pending. A skipped day is tracked separately from a recorded value.\n\nDaily plans support numeric or Checklist measures. A legacy Checklist target counts checked items and cannot exceed the number of items. Boolean measures do not have numeric planning targets. A daily target is not a threshold that decides whether the tracker’s overall success rule qualifies; configure those separately."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Cumulative deadline plan","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Cumulative deadline plan","content":"## Cumulative deadline plan\n\nA cumulative plan sets one total to reach by the tracker deadline, such as “complete 100 pages by the end of the month”. The deadline is required. The plan distributes expected progress across scheduled dates and shows actual progress, expected progress, remaining work, required daily pace, and a pace state such as ahead, on track, behind, overdue, or no scheduled days.\n\nCumulative planning can sum only measures explicitly configured as **Incremental**, where each entry adds new progress. A **Snapshot** is already a total, so adding snapshots across dates would count the same work repeatedly. A measure with an existing cumulative target cannot be changed to Snapshot until that target is resolved. Legacy Checklist entries contribute the count checked on each eligible entry and the cumulative total may span repeated scheduled days.\n\nRest days and holidays do not add scheduled pace opportunities. Recorded incremental progress on a rest date still represents real progress and can count toward the total. Today remains available for the plan until today’s entry is submitted; after a recorded or skipped entry, pace and allocation calculations use remaining eligible dates.\n\nIf there are no scheduled dates in the plan window, the plan reports that state instead of inventing a daily pace. A deadline before the effective start date is invalid. The effective start respects both the chosen start and the tracker’s creation date in the workspace time zone."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Allocation planning","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Allocation planning","content":"## Allocation planning\n\nThe allocation view can preview how a cumulative total could be spread across remaining scheduled dates. The calculated pace is a suggestion for planning; it is not itself a check-in, a saved entry, or a change to the goal total. Review the preview and the saved target separately. The total is measured in the selected measure’s unit."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Milestones","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Milestones","content":"## Milestones\n\nA milestone is a named checkpoint associated with a tracker and, when configured, a measure and value. It marks progress toward an outcome; it does not create another check-in or add separate progress. Boolean observations can be interpreted as 0/1, numeric observations use their nonnegative value, and a valid legacy Checklist observation uses the number of checked items. The comparison follows the configured milestone interpretation.\n\nIf a milestone refers to a measure, resolve that dependency before removing or retiring the measure. Retired measure definitions remain available for historical display, but they should not remain a dependency of an active plan that needs future inputs."},{"slug":"goals-and-milestones","title":"Goals, planning, and milestones: Examples and common mistakes","path":"docs/ai-help/goals-and-milestones.md","section":"Examples and common mistakes","content":"## Examples and common mistakes\n\n- **Repeated practice:** “Exercise 20 minutes on each scheduled day” is a daily recurring target.\n- **Finish a deliverable:** “Write 12,000 words by a deadline” is cumulative only if each entry records newly written words (incremental), not a running lifetime total (snapshot).\n- **Checkpoint:** “Draft complete at 5,000 words” can be a milestone on the relevant measure; it is not another daily target.\n- A per-check-in Target does not automatically become a daily or cumulative planning target.\n- Missing a daily target can lower plan consistency without deleting the recorded value.\n- If a cumulative plan appears behind, check the progress semantics, selected measure, schedule, active dates, deadline, holidays, and whether today’s entry has already closed the current opportunity.\n\nSource references: `src/domain/trackers/planning.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/planning.test.ts`, `src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx`, `src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.test.tsx`, `src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx`, `src/features/goals/GoalsPage.test.tsx`."},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync: Check-ins, History, Analytics, and synchronization","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","section":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and synchronization","content":"# Check-ins, History, Analytics, and synchronization"},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync: Check-in records and History","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","section":"Check-in records and History","content":"## Check-in records and History\n\nA check-in belongs to a tracker and date and stores values by stable measure ID. The tracker definition supplies the labels, units, and types used to interpret those values. Editing a measure with saved history is restricted so old values keep their meaning. Retiring the measure removes it from future check-in forms, but the definition remains for historical rendering.\n\nHistory lets you review recorded and skipped dates and see each saved measure value with its name and unit. A legacy Checklist is rendered as a checked-item count while its retained item states preserve the old context. Retired measures can still appear in past entries. The latest live revision for a date is used; deleted/tombstoned entries are not treated as current activity.\n\nTo troubleshoot a missing value, confirm the tracker and date filters, whether the check-in is recorded or skipped, whether a later revision replaced it, and whether an entry was deleted. Pausing or archiving a tracker does not erase its saved history."},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync: Analytics","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","section":"Analytics","content":"## Analytics\n\nAnalytics can summarize **All Trackers** or an individual tracker over the selected 7-, 30-, or 90-day window. Aggregate counts such as check-ins and eligible opportunities can be compared across trackers; values with different units are not combined. Each measure gets its own observation count, average, latest value, and dated trend. Boolean values are represented as yes/no observations; a Checklist is represented by the number of checked items.\n\nConsistency is qualified eligible opportunities divided by elapsed opportunities. The current unlogged day remains open and is not included as a missed opportunity. Standard Mode counts scheduled non-holiday dates; Strict Mode counts every active calendar day. Rest days and holidays are excluded in Standard Mode and required in Strict Mode. The tracker’s active date range and schedule constrain opportunities. A recorded value may be present in the metric trend without qualifying toward consistency if it fails the success rule.\n\nRetired measures remain part of historical metric summaries because their definitions are retained. Analytics does not combine their observations with another measure or unit."},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync: Local storage and cloud synchronization","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","section":"Local storage and cloud synchronization","content":"## Local storage and cloud synchronization\n\nThe browser saves workspace data locally first. When signed in and online, queued tracker, entry, and holiday changes synchronize with Supabase. Revision tracking detects when a cloud record has changed since the local device last read it. The app preserves both sides in a sync conflict instead of silently overwriting one version.\n\nTracker sync checks stable measure IDs and historical interpretation. A remote edit that changes the type of a saved measure or the meaning of a measure with recorded history becomes a conflict. Resolve it through the app’s conflict flow before making dependent edits or deleting the tracker. Offline changes remain queued locally until sync can proceed.\n\nThe sync engine verifies account ownership and rechecks the active account while applying pages of remote data. It does not merge records owned by another account. If sync is pending, failed, or conflicted, check the connection and sync status, then resolve the listed conflict. Do not delete local data to “fix” a conflict; that can remove the preserved local version.\n\nWorkspace appearance and time-zone preferences are local settings and do not currently synchronize. Date-only check-ins remain on their original dates when the time zone changes; future date interpretation uses the selected zone."},{"slug":"history-analytics-sync","title":"Check-ins, History, Analytics, and sync: Examples and common questions","path":"docs/ai-help/history-analytics-sync.md","section":"Examples and common questions","content":"## Examples and common questions\n\n- **“Why does the old measure still appear in History?”** Retirement preserves the definition so earlier entries keep their original label and unit.\n- **“Why is there no old value in Analytics?”** Check whether the selected date period includes it, whether the measure had a value on that date, and whether the entry is the latest live revision.\n- **“Why did an edit not overwrite the other device?”** The remote revision changed; the app records a conflict so the two definitions can be reviewed.\n- **“Why does All Trackers not show one combined number?”** Different measures may use different units, so trends and values remain separated by measure.\n\nSource references: `src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx`, `src/features/history/HistoryPage.test.tsx`, `src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts`, `src/domain/trackers/activityHeatmap.ts`, `src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts`, `src/services/supabase/syncEngine.test.ts`, `src/db/syncConflictRepository.ts`, `src/db/localRepository.ts`, `src/db/database.ts`, `src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx`."}] as const
export const verifiedQuestionCatalog = [{"id":"offline-sync","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Can I use ProgressTracker without internet?","aliases":["What happens when I go offline?","Will my changes sync later?","Can I use this without internet?"],"keywords":["offline","local","sync","internet","device"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx"],"answer":"Tracker data is stored locally in the browser, so you can continue working while offline. Signed-in account data synchronizes when a connection is available again. Until then, changes on that device may not appear elsewhere."},{"id":"cross-device-sync","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Will my progress appear on another device?","aliases":["How do I sync trackers between devices?","Can I access my data on a new device?"],"keywords":["account","sign in","sync","devices","cloud"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts"],"answer":"Cross-device synchronization is available when you sign in to the same account and the devices are online. Guest data is stored locally on the device and does not automatically appear on another device."},{"id":"sync-conflicts","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens if two devices edit the same day?","aliases":["How does sync handle conflicting edits?","Will ProgressTracker merge two versions automatically?"],"keywords":["conflict","revision","sync","devices","edit"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.test.ts"],"answer":"When edits cannot be reconciled safely, sync records a conflict for you to resolve instead of silently combining incompatible versions. Review the conflict in the app’s sync/conflict flow; do not assume both edits were merged."},{"id":"account-signin","category":"accounts-sync","question":"How do I sign in or create an account?","aliases":["Can I sign in with an email link?","How do I register?"],"keywords":["sign in","create account","email link","password","authentication"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx","src/features/auth/authService.ts","src/features/auth/AuthPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Use the account screen to request an email sign-in link or choose password sign-in. Choose Create account when registering a new account; using an email sign-in link for the first time creates an account for that email."},{"id":"workspace-backup","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Can I back up or restore my workspace data?","aliases":["How do I export my progress?","Can I import a workspace backup?"],"keywords":["backup","export","restore","JSON","workspace","sync conflicts"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/WorkspaceBackup.tsx","src/db/workspaceBackup.ts","src/db/workspaceBackup.test.ts"],"answer":"Settings provides a local workspace backup you can download as JSON and restore into the same guest workspace or account. Restore previews changes, adds missing records, skips identical records, and stops if it finds a conflicting ID or date. Keep the backup file private."},{"id":"signout-local-data","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens to local workspace data when I sign out?","aliases":["Does signing out erase check-ins from this device?","Will my local progress remain after sign-out?"],"keywords":["sign out","local workspace","check-ins","data","account"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"Signing out ends the account session; it does not itself delete the local workspace records. Account data remains associated with its local workspace, and the app uses a workspace-selection step when choosing guest data after sign-out."},{"id":"offline-sync-later","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What happens to a check-in I save while offline?","aliases":["Will my offline entry upload when I reconnect?","Does a disconnected check-in stay on this device?"],"keywords":["offline check-in","pending sync","reconnect","local storage"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx"],"answer":"The check-in is saved locally and its account-sync work remains pending until a connection is available. It may not appear on another device before synchronization completes."},{"id":"sync-deletion","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Does clearing a check-in sync to my other devices?","aliases":["Will a cleared entry disappear from my other device?","Does a check-in deletion upload when I reconnect?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","sync","other devices","deletion marker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts"],"answer":"For a signed-in account, clearing queues a deletion update for synchronization. Other devices reflect the change after they synchronize with the account; while offline, they may still show their earlier local copy."},{"id":"sync-conflict-preserves-versions","category":"accounts-sync","question":"What information is kept when two device edits conflict?","aliases":["Does sync keep both versions of a conflict?","Can ProgressTracker merge conflicting tracker changes automatically?"],"keywords":["sync conflict","local version","remote version","revision","resolution"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.ts","src/db/syncConflictRepository.test.ts"],"answer":"When a revision conflict cannot be reconciled safely, the sync flow records the conflicting local and remote data for you to resolve. It does not silently blend incompatible changes. Review the conflict before choosing which version to keep."},{"id":"sync-preference-scope","category":"accounts-sync","question":"Do workspace time zone and appearance settings sync between devices?","aliases":["Will my theme and calendar time zone follow me to another device?","Are workspace display preferences stored in my account?"],"keywords":["settings","time zone","appearance","sync","devices"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/features/settings/appearance.ts","src/features/settings/UnifiedSettings.test.tsx"],"answer":"No. The workspace time zone and appearance preferences are stored locally and currently do not synchronize between devices. Set them separately in each workspace."},{"id":"ai-help-private-data","category":"ai-help","question":"Can AI Help see my tracker entries?","aliases":["Does Groq receive my personal progress?","What data is sent when I ask a question?","Can AI Help read my check-in values?"],"keywords":["privacy","tracker entries","personal data","Groq","AI Help"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/index.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/assistantCore.ts"],"answer":"AI Help answers questions about how the product works; its request includes your question and limited conversation context, not your tracker entries. Do not include private tracker details in a question or support message."},{"id":"ai-help-suggested-offline","category":"ai-help","question":"Can I use suggested AI Help questions while offline?","aliases":["Do the suggested questions work without internet?","Can AI Help show a saved answer if I am disconnected?"],"keywords":["AI Help","suggestions","offline","verified answer","internet"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","src/features/ai-help/AIHelpAssistant.tsx"],"answer":"Yes, a displayed verified suggestion opens its bundled answer without a network request. Manually typed questions need a connection for the full retrieval service; only questions matched by the smaller local help catalog can receive a local answer offline."},{"id":"ai-help-typed-retrieval","category":"ai-help","question":"How does AI Help handle a question I type myself?","aliases":["Does free-form Ask ProgressTracker use the verified answers?","What happens when I ask a question that is not a suggestion?"],"keywords":["AI Help","typed question","free-form","knowledge retrieval","source evidence"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/ai-help/aiHelpService.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/index.ts","supabase/functions/ai-help/assistantCore.ts"],"answer":"When online, a typed question is checked against verified Q&A first. If no clear catalog answer applies, the service can use relevant product documentation and reviewed source evidence to form a grounded answer. AI Help does not receive your tracker entries."},{"id":"calendar-content","category":"calendar","question":"What does the calendar show?","aliases":["What do the calendar colors mean?","Can I see progress by date?"],"keywords":["calendar","activity","status","heatmap","date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityHeatmap.ts"],"answer":"The calendar lets you navigate dates and review tracker activity for the selected period. Its date indicators summarize scheduled opportunities and saved progress; open a date to review or update the entries available for that day. Use the information button beside Status guide for the difference between saved outcomes and derived statuses, and how holidays, tracker periods, All Trackers, and streak qualification affect the summary."},{"id":"calendar-activity-statuses","category":"calendar","question":"What do the Calendar activity statuses mean?","aliases":["What is the difference between pending, missed, and no progress?","What do the status labels in Calendar mean?"],"keywords":["Calendar","status","pending","missed","completed","historical"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"Completed means a saved recorded check-in met the configured completion rule, but completion does not always mean it qualifies for a streak. Partial and No progress are saved outcomes; Skipped is an intentional saved outcome. Pending, Missed, Upcoming, Rest day, Outside period, Historical entry, Holiday, Tracker inactive, and No active trackers are derived from saved data and date, schedule, mode, or tracker context. Standard Mode treats holidays as neutral, while Strict Mode still requires activity on an active date. Rest day can also describe an in-period date outside the tracker’s schedule; dates before the effective start or after a deadline are Outside period. The Status guide’s information button explains these distinctions. In All Trackers, a date summarizes active trackers; mixed statuses are marked on the cell and selecting the date shows each tracker’s result. The summary and saved-entry count use that same tracker scope. Selecting one tracker, including a paused or archived tracker, shows its retained activity."},{"id":"calendar-inspect-past-date","category":"calendar","question":"How do I inspect tracker activity on a past date?","aliases":["Can I open a previous day in Calendar?","Where can I see what happened on a particular date?"],"keywords":["Calendar","past date","select date","activity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Open Calendar, navigate to the month, and select the date. The selected-day panel shows statuses and saved values by tracker; use its History link to review an entry or its check-in action when available."},{"id":"calendar-rest-day","category":"calendar","question":"How do rest days appear in Calendar?","aliases":["Does Calendar show unscheduled tracker days?","What status does an off day have?"],"keywords":["Calendar","rest day","unscheduled","tracker schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, an in-period date excluded by the active tracker’s schedule is a Rest day. Strict Mode makes every in-period date an opportunity, including schedule rest days. Dates before the effective start or after the deadline are Outside period, not Rest days. Saved check-ins remain visible on rest days and outside the active period."},{"id":"calendar-zero-activity","category":"calendar","question":"Does a recorded zero count as activity in Calendar?","aliases":["Is zero different from no check-in on the calendar?","Why is my zero entry not marked completed?"],"keywords":["Calendar","zero","quantity","recorded","success rule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"A saved zero is a recorded value, so it is different from an empty date. Whether the day is Completed depends on the tracker’s success rule; zero may be recorded without qualifying, and the Calendar can show No progress."},{"id":"calendar-holiday-entry","category":"calendar","question":"Does a saved check-in stay visible on a holiday?","aliases":["Does marking a holiday hide progress already recorded?","Can a holiday date still show my check-in?"],"keywords":["Calendar","holiday","saved check-in","retain","workspace"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"Yes. The selected-day details and History retain saved check-ins. Standard Mode’s holiday marker can appear alongside the saved outcome; Strict Mode still requires activity, so a missing past check-in can be Missed on a holiday."},{"id":"heatmap-normalized","category":"calendar","question":"What does the Insights heatmap measure?","aliases":["How are the heatmap colors calculated?","Does one heatmap shade mean one check-in?"],"keywords":["heatmap","eligible opportunities","qualifying check-ins","percent","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityHeatmap.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx"],"answer":"For each date, the heatmap compares qualifying check-ins with eligible opportunities and colors the result by that day’s percentage. In an all-tracker view, it combines opportunity counts across active trackers while applying each tracker’s Standard or Strict Mode rules."},{"id":"calendar-versus-history","category":"calendar","question":"Why does Calendar show dates that I do not see in History?","aliases":["What is the difference between Calendar and History?","Why is an empty date on Calendar missing from my History list?"],"keywords":["Calendar","History","activity status","saved check-ins","missing"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Calendar summarizes tracker status across selected dates, including pending, missed, holiday, and rest days. History lists saved check-ins and holidays in its selected range, with a separate recent missing-opportunity review; an empty calendar date is not necessarily a saved history entry."},{"id":"skipped-vs-unchecked","category":"check-ins","question":"What is the difference between a skipped and unchecked day?","aliases":["Is skipping the same as leaving a day blank?","What does an unchecked date mean?","What is the difference between skipped and not checked?"],"keywords":["skipped","unchecked","absent","missing check-in","outcome"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"A skipped day is an explicitly saved check-in marked as skipped. An unchecked past date has no saved entry and is shown as Missed only if it was a required opportunity. A saved recorded check-in that fails its success rule remains distinct: it appears as Partial when it has positive progress, or No progress when it does not. Missed is derived and is never saved automatically."},{"id":"edit-past-checkin","category":"check-ins","question":"Can I edit a past check-in?","aliases":["Can I change yesterday’s progress?","How do I correct an old entry?"],"keywords":["history","edit","past date","check-in","values"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"Yes. Open History, select the saved date and tracker entry, then edit its values. The latest saved revision for that date is used in current calculations."},{"id":"clear-checkin","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens if I clear a check-in?","aliases":["Can I undo a check-in?","What happens if I clear yesterday’s progress?"],"keywords":["clear","delete","history","missing","re-record","check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/shared/ClearCheckInAction.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"Clearing removes the saved check-in from current progress calculations. If that date was a past opportunity, it can then appear in missing check-in review. You can record the date again by creating a new check-in."},{"id":"numeric-zero-vs-empty","category":"check-ins","question":"Is entering zero different from leaving a number blank?","aliases":["Does zero count as no progress?","Is a blank quantity treated as zero?"],"keywords":["quantity","zero","blank","observation","numeric"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/schema.ts"],"answer":"Yes. Zero is a recorded numeric value and can be included in observations. A blank field is not a numeric observation. Whether a recorded zero qualifies as a successful check-in depends on the tracker’s success rules."},{"id":"mark-missed","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens when I mark a check-in as skipped?","aliases":["Is marking a day missed different from leaving it blank?","Does Mark as skipped break my streak?"],"keywords":["mark as skipped","skipped","outcome","unchecked","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx"],"answer":"Mark as skipped saves an intentional skipped outcome for that date. It is not the same as a derived Missed date or a saved No progress result. On a required opportunity, it does not qualify for a streak. Leaving a date unchecked creates no saved entry; after a required date elapses, it can appear as Missed."},{"id":"custom-checkin-fields","category":"check-ins","question":"What are custom check-in fields?","aliases":["Can I add a note to a check-in?","Do notes count toward goal progress?"],"keywords":["notes","custom fields","context","measure","goal progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.test.tsx"],"answer":"Custom check-in fields add context to an entry, such as a note or selected answer. They are separate from tracker measures and are not used as numeric goal totals."},{"id":"checkin-types","category":"check-ins","question":"What kinds of values can I record in a tracker?","aliases":["Can I track a number or a yes/no habit?","What measure types are available?"],"keywords":["Yes/No","quantity","measures","recorded values","legacy"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/features/trackers/trackerSetupSchema.ts","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx"],"answer":"New tracker measures use Yes/No or Quantity values. Existing trackers may also contain legacy measure types such as Duration or Checklist, which remain supported for their saved history."},{"id":"checkin-empty-versus-zero-status","category":"check-ins","question":"Why can a saved zero show no progress instead of a missed day?","aliases":["Is a zero entry treated as unchecked?","How does Calendar distinguish zero from no check-in?"],"keywords":["zero","no progress","missed","saved entry","activity status"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx"],"answer":"A saved zero is still a check-in, not a missed day. Calendar evaluates it against the tracker’s success rule and may show No progress; if the rule explicitly accepts zero, it can show Completed. Missed means an elapsed required opportunity has no active saved check-in. An open opportunity today is Pending, and a future opportunity is Upcoming."},{"id":"checkin-resave-same-date","category":"check-ins","question":"What happens if I save a check-in again for the same date?","aliases":["Can a tracker have two check-ins on one day?","Does saving another entry replace my check-in for that date?"],"keywords":["same date","edit","save","latest revision","check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The app keeps one active check-in per tracker and date. Saving again updates that date’s entry, and calculations use the latest live revision rather than adding a second daily record."},{"id":"checkin-note-vs-measure","category":"check-ins","question":"Does a check-in note count as a measure value?","aliases":["Can a note contribute to my numeric goal?","Are custom answers included in tracker statistics?"],"keywords":["note","custom field","measure","metric","goal progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/shared/TrackerEntryFields.tsx","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts"],"answer":"No. A note or custom check-in answer adds context to the entry. Goal calculations and measure statistics use tracker measure values, not those custom fields."},{"id":"guest-mode","category":"getting-started","question":"Can I use ProgressTracker as a guest?","aliases":["Do I need an account to start tracking?","What happens to guest data?"],"keywords":["guest","account","local storage","sign in","tracker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/auth/AuthProvider.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/auth/AuthPage.tsx","src/features/auth/AuthProvider.test.tsx"],"answer":"You can use ProgressTracker without signing in. Guest tracker data is stored locally in the browser on that device. Signing in enables account synchronization, but guest data does not automatically appear on another device."},{"id":"create-tracker","category":"getting-started","question":"How do I create a tracker?","aliases":["How do I start tracking a habit?","Where do I add a new tracker?"],"keywords":["create","setup","habit","goal","schedule","measure"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.test.tsx","src/features/trackers/trackerSetupSchema.ts"],"answer":"Open Trackers and choose Create tracker. Give it a name, choose the tracker kind and measures, then set its schedule and active dates. Save the form to begin using it. New measures support Yes/No or Quantity; some existing trackers can retain legacy measure types."},{"id":"daily-vs-cumulative-goal","category":"goals","question":"What is the difference between daily and cumulative goals?","aliases":["How does cumulative progress work?","Does my goal target reset every day?"],"keywords":["daily plan","cumulative plan","target","allocations","progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts","src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx"],"answer":"A daily plan sets a target for each planned day. A cumulative plan sets a total amount to reach across its date range, with progress allocated across the plan. Which model applies depends on the saved goal plan."},{"id":"milestones","category":"goals","question":"How are milestones calculated?","aliases":["When is a milestone reached?","What does a linked milestone mean?"],"keywords":["goal","milestone","target","progress","linked measure"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/allocationPreview.ts","src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx"],"answer":"A milestone is reached when the progress used by its linked goal plan meets the milestone target. The exact progress comes from that goal’s daily or cumulative plan and its eligible recorded values."},{"id":"goal-deadline","category":"goals","question":"Can a goal have a deadline?","aliases":["How does a goal deadline work?","What happens when a goal’s end date passes?"],"keywords":["goal","deadline","cumulative","active period","target"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"Yes. A goal can use a deadline to bound its planned date range, especially for cumulative targets. Progress and pacing are calculated within that plan period; dates after the tracker deadline are not included in its cumulative progress."},{"id":"complete-goal","category":"goals","question":"When is a goal complete?","aliases":["How do I know I reached my goal target?","Does reaching a milestone complete the goal?"],"keywords":["goal","completed","target","progress","milestone"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"The goal plan reports its target as complete when no planned work remains. The Goals page also shows the tracker’s saved status, so the displayed status can depend on both the goal state and plan. A milestone is a checkpoint within a plan; reaching one does not by itself mean the overall target is complete."},{"id":"goal-daily-missing","category":"goals","question":"How does a daily goal plan treat a missing date?","aliases":["Does a missed day count as meeting my daily target?","What happens to a daily target when I do not check in?"],"keywords":["daily goal","missing","missed","target","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"A past scheduled date without a usable check-in is treated as missed in the daily plan. Today remains pending while it is still open, and rest days, holidays, and future dates are shown separately rather than as missed opportunities."},{"id":"goal-cumulative-snapshot","category":"goals","question":"Do snapshot check-ins add together toward a cumulative goal?","aliases":["Are repeated snapshot values summed for a total goal?","Which entries count toward cumulative progress?"],"keywords":["cumulative goal","snapshot","incremental","total progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/goalPlanning.test.ts"],"answer":"No. Cumulative progress sums entries configured as incremental. Snapshot values describe a level at a point in time and are not added together across dates."},{"id":"goal-clearing-entry","category":"goals","question":"Does clearing a check-in change goal progress?","aliases":["Will a deleted entry reduce my goal total?","Does removing a historical check-in recalculate the goal?","Can clearing a check-in change my goal progress?","Will my goal total go down if I clear an entry?","Does removing a check-in update the Goals page?"],"keywords":["goal progress","clear check-in","delete entry","recalculate"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Goal progress is calculated from active saved entries, so clearing a check-in can change the displayed progress or pacing. The effect depends on the plan and whether that entry contributes a qualifying value."},{"id":"goal-target-change","category":"goals","question":"What happens if I change a goal target?","aliases":["Does editing my target change saved check-ins?","Will a new goal target recalculate my plan?"],"keywords":["goal target","edit plan","recalculation","saved progress"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The plan and its remaining pace are recalculated against the new target and existing saved progress. Changing the target does not rewrite the check-ins themselves."},{"id":"goal-metric-unit","category":"goals","question":"Where does a goal’s unit come from?","aliases":["How does a goal know whether progress is pages or minutes?","Can I choose a different unit for goal progress?"],"keywords":["goal","measure","unit","metric","quantity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/goals/GoalsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/GoalPlanningEditor.tsx"],"answer":"The goal uses the unit of its linked tracker measure. Choose or edit the measure’s unit in tracker configuration; the goal plan displays values in that unit rather than converting them."},{"id":"history-includes","category":"history","question":"What does History include?","aliases":["What can I see in History?","Why does History not show every date?","Where can I review saved check-ins?"],"keywords":["saved entries","historical","holidays","missing check-ins","date","values"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"History shows saved check-ins and their recorded values for past dates, along with workspace holidays in the selected date range. It also offers a missing check-in review for unresolved opportunities in the previous seven completed days. Dates that were not tracking opportunities are not shown as missing, and today is not treated as overdue."},{"id":"history-clear-note","category":"history","question":"Does clearing a check-in remove its note?","aliases":["Does clearing remove a check-in note?","What happens to a note when I clear its check-in?","Is the note kept if I delete an old entry?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","note","history","deleted entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"The note belongs to the saved check-in, so clearing the check-in removes it from active History along with the entry. Clearing does not provide a separate option to keep the note while removing the check-in."},{"id":"history-clear-sync","category":"history","question":"Is clearing a check-in the same as permanently erasing it everywhere?","aliases":["Does clearing permanently delete a check-in from storage?","Is a cleared entry removed from the cloud too?"],"keywords":["clear","permanent deletion","tombstone","sync","history"],"suggestible":false,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Clearing removes the entry from active history on this device and queues a deletion update for account sync when available. The app uses deletion state during synchronization; clearing should not be treated as proof that every stored copy or backup has been permanently erased."},{"id":"history-reenter-cleared","category":"history","question":"Are my old values restored when I check in again after clearing?","aliases":["Can I undo a cleared check-in by logging again?","What if I want to add progress on that date after clearing it?"],"keywords":["clear","re-enter","save","check-in","date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. Clearing removes the entry from active history, so its old values are not filled back into a new check-in. You can save progress for that tracker and date again by entering the values you want to record."},{"id":"history-cleared-missing","category":"history","question":"Why can a cleared date appear as a missing check-in?","aliases":["Does clearing make an old scheduled day missing?","Why did History list a date after I removed its entry?"],"keywords":["clear","missing check-in","scheduled opportunity","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"The missing-check-in review looks for past opportunities without an active saved entry. After you clear an entry, a past date can qualify as missing if it is still an active opportunity under that tracker’s schedule, mode, and holiday rules."},{"id":"history-clear-streak","category":"history","question":"Does clearing a check-in affect my streak?","aliases":["Will deleting a past entry recalculate my streak?","What happens to a streak after I clear one day?"],"keywords":["clear check-in","streak","recalculation","opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"Yes, streaks are calculated from active saved entries, so clearing one can change the current or longest streak. The result depends on whether that date is a counted opportunity under Standard or Strict Mode and the tracker’s schedule and holiday rules."},{"id":"history-outside-period","category":"history","question":"Why does History label an entry as outside the tracker period?","aliases":["What does Historical mean next to an old check-in?","Why is my saved entry not counted in current progress?"],"keywords":["History","historical entry","start date","deadline","active period"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The entry was saved on a date outside the tracker’s current active period, which is bounded by its effective start date and deadline. History keeps the entry visible, but it does not count toward current period calculations."},{"id":"history-seven-day-review","category":"history","question":"How far back does History review missing check-ins?","aliases":["Can History find older missed dates?","Does the missing section cover the whole tracker history?"],"keywords":["History","missing check-ins","seven days","review window"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"The missing check-in section reviews unresolved opportunities in the previous seven completed days. It is a short review window, not a list of every gap in the tracker’s history; use Calendar to inspect older dates."},{"id":"history-cleared-holiday","category":"history","question":"Can a cleared check-in on a holiday become a missing date?","aliases":["Will clearing a holiday entry create a missed check-in?","Does the missing review include holidays after I clear them?"],"keywords":["cleared check-in","holiday","missing","Strict Mode","Standard Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.test.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, holidays are excluded from scheduled opportunities, so a cleared holiday entry is not listed as missing. Strict Mode treats every active date, including holidays, as an opportunity; a past cleared holiday can therefore appear in the missing review."},{"id":"missing-checkins","category":"history","question":"Where can I find missing check-ins?","aliases":["How do I review missed days?","Can I find dates I forgot to log?","Where do I review missed check-ins?"],"keywords":["missing","overdue","history","schedule","past opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/missingCheckIns.ts"],"answer":"Open History and review its missing check-in section. It lists past unresolved opportunities for active trackers, based on each tracker’s active dates, schedule, Strict Mode, and workspace holidays. It does not list today as missing."},{"id":"create-holiday","category":"holidays","question":"How do I add a holiday?","aliases":["Can I mark a day as a break?","How do I add a retroactive holiday?"],"keywords":["holiday","break","date","reason","workspace"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx","src/domain/holidays.ts","src/domain/holidays.test.ts"],"answer":"Open Holidays & breaks, choose a date, and save the holiday. You can add a reason and choose a past date; holidays apply across the workspace rather than to only one tracker. To change a saved holiday, open its three-dot menu and choose Edit holiday. Update the date, reason, or both. The edit keeps the same holiday record and syncs across devices when signed in."},{"id":"delete-holiday","category":"holidays","question":"What happens if I delete a holiday?","aliases":["Does removing a holiday change saved check-ins?","Can I undo a workspace break?"],"keywords":["holiday","delete","saved check-in","schedule","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx","src/domain/holidays.ts"],"answer":"Deleting a holiday removes that date’s break from future calculations and moves it to Recently deleted holidays, where it can be restored for 30 days. When permanent deletion is enabled for the deployment, you can also confirm that action from the holiday’s three-dot menu. Any check-ins already saved for the date remain saved; deleting the holiday does not erase them."},{"id":"holidays-streaks","category":"holidays","question":"Do holidays count against my streak?","aliases":["How do holidays affect scheduled check-ins?","Does a holiday pause my tracker?","Do holidays count against my streak?"],"keywords":["holiday","streak","scheduled","strict mode","recorded entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/holidays.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, a holiday removes that date from scheduled streak opportunities. In Strict Mode, dates remain daily opportunities, so a holiday by itself does not excuse a missed day. A saved check-in remains visible in either mode; a qualifying one counts in Strict Mode. Goal plans use their own schedule rules."},{"id":"holiday-all-trackers","category":"holidays","question":"Do workspace holidays apply to every tracker?","aliases":["Can I make a holiday for just one tracker?","Is a holiday shared across my trackers?"],"keywords":["workspace holiday","all trackers","schedule","break"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/holidays.ts","src/features/holidays/HolidaysPage.tsx"],"answer":"Yes. Holidays are workspace-wide dates, not tracker-specific settings. Tracker opportunity behavior depends on mode: Standard Mode pauses scheduled opportunities, while Strict Mode counts every active date. Goal plans account for holidays according to their own planning rules."},{"id":"holiday-remove-recalculates","category":"holidays","question":"What changes when I remove a holiday?","aliases":["Does deleting a holiday make that date count again?","Will removing a holiday change my streak or statistics?"],"keywords":["holiday","remove","schedule","recalculate","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/holidays.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts"],"answer":"Removing the holiday makes the date subject to the tracker’s usual mode and schedule rules again. Calculated streaks and statistics can therefore change, but saved check-ins are not removed."},{"id":"holiday-log-progress","category":"holidays","question":"Can I record progress on a holiday?","aliases":["Are check-ins allowed during a workspace break?","Can I voluntarily log on a holiday?"],"keywords":["holiday","voluntary check-in","saved entry","calendar"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/calendar/CalendarPage.tsx","src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"Yes. A holiday does not prevent a check-in from being saved. Calendar offers a voluntary check-in on an active tracker’s holiday, and the saved entry remains visible. In Standard Mode, the entry is saved and included in applicable metrics, but the holiday does not add a scheduled streak opportunity. In Strict Mode, the holiday remains a required opportunity, and the entry counts toward the streak only if it meets the tracker’s streak qualification."},{"id":"holiday-standard-v-strict","category":"holidays","question":"Why can a holiday be missed in Strict Mode?","aliases":["Why does Strict Mode still expect a check-in on a holiday?","Does Strict Mode pause for workspace holidays?"],"keywords":["Strict Mode","holiday","opportunity","missed","streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Strict Mode treats every date in the tracker’s active period as an opportunity, including holidays. Without a qualifying check-in, an elapsed holiday can break the streak. Standard Mode excludes holidays from scheduled opportunities."},{"id":"insight-tracker-cards","category":"insights","question":"What does the Your Trackers section show?","aliases":["What are the tracker cards in Insights?","What information appears on an Insights tracker card?"],"keywords":["Insights","tracker cards","current date","status","streak","latest check-in"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Each active tracker card is a snapshot for the workspace-local current date. It shows today’s status, that tracker’s current streak and personal best, and its latest saved check-in with that entry’s date, outcome, and values. These refer to separate dates and purposes."},{"id":"insight-all-trackers-streak","category":"insights","question":"What does the All Trackers streak on Insights measure?","aliases":["Is All Trackers streak the sum of tracker streaks?","How is my Perfect Day streak calculated?"],"keywords":["Insights","All Trackers streak","Perfect Day","account streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts"],"answer":"It is the consecutive run of account days on which every required tracker qualifies, with at least one required tracker that day. It is not a sum of separate tracker streaks. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral; Strict Mode dates within a tracker’s active period require a qualifying check-in. A pending current day does not prematurely break the confirmed run."},{"id":"insight-current-status","category":"insights","question":"Does an Insights tracker card show today or my latest check-in?","aliases":["What date does a tracker card represent?","Is the status on my tracker card from today or my last entry?"],"keywords":["Insights","snapshot date","current status","latest saved entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"The card’s status and streak are a snapshot as of today in your workspace time zone. The separate “Latest check-in” area shows the newest saved entry and its actual date, which may be earlier."},{"id":"insight-latest-checkin","category":"insights","question":"What does the latest check-in date on an Insights card mean?","aliases":["Does latest check-in mean I logged today?","Why is the check-in date on my card from an earlier day?"],"keywords":["latest check-in","saved entry","date","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"It is the date of the most recent active saved check-in for that tracker. It does not imply that you checked in today. Cleared entries are excluded; if no active entry exists, the card says “No check-ins yet.”"},{"id":"insight-empty-tracker","category":"insights","question":"Why does an Insights card say no check-ins yet?","aliases":["What does “No check-ins yet” mean on my tracker?","Why is there no latest entry on a tracker card?"],"keywords":["Insights","empty tracker","no check-ins","latest entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"There is no active saved check-in for that tracker. Today’s status is shown separately, so a holiday or rest day does not mean an unfinished check-in; it describes today’s tracking status."},{"id":"insight-streak-personal-best","category":"insights","question":"What do current streak and personal best mean on an Insights card?","aliases":["What is the personal best on my tracker card?","How are the two streak numbers on Insights different?"],"keywords":["current streak","personal best","longest streak","Insights"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Current streak is the qualifying run through today under the tracker’s mode. Personal best is the longest qualifying run in its saved history. Standard Mode lets holidays and rest days preserve continuity without adding to the count; Strict Mode requires a qualifying entry on every active calendar date, including holidays and rest days."},{"id":"insight-holiday-status","category":"insights","question":"Why does today’s card status differ from my latest check-in?","aliases":["Why does Insights show a holiday when my last entry was completed?","Can the latest check-in and today’s status be different?"],"keywords":["Insights","today","holiday","latest check-in","current status"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/activityStatus.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Today’s status and the latest saved check-in describe different dates. A holiday can be today’s workspace status while the latest check-in remains an earlier entry; the card labels that entry with its own date and outcome."},{"id":"insight-timezone-date","category":"insights","question":"Which time zone determines the date shown in Insights?","aliases":["Is the Insights snapshot date local to my workspace?","Why does the Insights date change around midnight?"],"keywords":["Insights","workspace time zone","snapshot date","midnight"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/db/calendarDate.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx"],"answer":"Insights uses the current date in the workspace’s selected time zone. Because that date can differ from UTC or your device’s other time zone, the snapshot may change at a different midnight."},{"id":"reminder-limits","category":"notifications","question":"Do reminders arrive when the app is closed?","aliases":["Are reminders sent in the background?","Why did I not get a push notification?"],"keywords":["notification","reminder","foreground","background","push"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/capabilities.ts"],"answer":"The current reminder monitor works while the app is open in the foreground. Background delivery depends on separate push delivery setup, so browser permission alone does not guarantee a reminder when the app is closed."},{"id":"notification-preferences","category":"notifications","question":"Where can I change notification preferences?","aliases":["How do I turn reminders on or off?","Can I change reminder settings?"],"keywords":["reminders","notifications","settings","browser permission"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx","src/features/notifications/capabilities.ts","src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.test.tsx"],"answer":"Open Settings and find Notifications to review the available reminder preferences and device permission status. Available controls depend on browser and device support."},{"id":"missing-checkin-reminder","category":"notifications","question":"How does the missing check-in reminder work?","aliases":["Why does Today show a missing check-in reminder?","When are overdue check-ins highlighted?"],"keywords":["Today","missing check-in","overdue","reminder","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/today/TodayPage.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.test.ts"],"answer":"The app can highlight unresolved opportunities for active trackers in its foreground experience, and History reviews missing opportunities from the previous seven completed days. These reminders depend on tracker schedules and active dates; archived and Bin trackers are not actionable reminders, and a reminder does not mean a saved check-in was deleted."},{"id":"reminder-previous-day-only","category":"notifications","question":"How far back does the overdue reminder look?","aliases":["Does the reminder scan all old missed days?","Will it notify me about every historical gap?"],"keywords":["overdue reminder","yesterday","historical","missed check-ins"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts"],"answer":"The overdue reminder checks unresolved required opportunities from yesterday. It does not scan every historical date. Future opportunities are Upcoming and do not trigger overdue reminders. History separately offers a review of missing opportunities from the previous seven completed days."},{"id":"reminder-dismissal","category":"notifications","question":"Does dismissing a missing check-in reminder complete the date?","aliases":["If I close a reminder, is the check-in marked done?","Does dismissing a notification resolve the missed day?"],"keywords":["dismiss reminder","mark complete","check-in","notification"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/db/localRepository.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts"],"answer":"No. Dismissing a notification changes the reminder’s read state; it does not create a check-in or mark the date complete. The date’s progress status changes only when you save or edit a check-in."},{"id":"reminder-foreground-check","category":"notifications","question":"Why do reminders run only while ProgressTracker is open?","aliases":["Does the app check for reminders in the background?","Why did no reminder arrive after I closed the app?"],"keywords":["foreground","background","scheduler","reminders","app open"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx"],"answer":"The reminder monitor evaluates reminders while the signed-in app is active. The Settings page reports that closed-app delivery still requires server-side sending and scheduling setup, so enabling device permission alone does not provide background reminders."},{"id":"reminder-timezone-quiet","category":"notifications","question":"Which time zone and quiet hours affect reminders?","aliases":["Are notification times based on my workspace time zone?","Why was a reminder delayed during quiet hours?"],"keywords":["reminder time","workspace time zone","quiet hours","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/NotificationsSettings.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx"],"answer":"Reminder times use the workspace time zone. Quiet hours suppress daily and motivation reminders; overdue reminders also pause during quiet hours unless their exception is enabled."},{"id":"reminder-repeats-unresolved","category":"notifications","question":"Why can I get another reminder for the same unresolved date?","aliases":["Why did dismissing a reminder not stop later reminders?","Can reminders repeat while I have not checked in?"],"keywords":["reminder","repeats","unresolved","daily schedule","dismissal"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/notifications/ForegroundReminderMonitor.tsx","src/features/notifications/reminderRules.ts","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"Daily reminders are evaluated at their configured times while the app is active. Dismissing one marks that notification as read; it does not resolve the opportunity, so a later scheduled reminder can still appear while the check-in remains unresolved."},{"id":"local-settings","category":"settings-privacy","question":"Do my appearance and time zone settings sync?","aliases":["Will dark mode carry to another device?","Does changing my time zone sync to my account?"],"keywords":["appearance","time zone","settings","local","sync"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/appearance.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/services/supabase/syncEngine.ts","src/features/settings/appearance.test.ts","src/features/settings/WorkspaceAppearance.test.tsx"],"answer":"Appearance and workspace time-zone preferences are stored locally and are not part of the account records synchronized between devices. Set them separately on each device where you use the app."},{"id":"timezone-dates","category":"settings-privacy","question":"Do check-in dates change when I change my time zone?","aliases":["Will my old entries move to a different day?","How does the workspace time zone affect tracking?"],"keywords":["time zone","calendar date","historical","check-in","local date"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/settings/WorkspaceTimeZone.tsx","src/db/calendarDate.ts","src/db/calendarDate.test.ts"],"answer":"Check-ins are stored by calendar date, so changing the workspace time zone does not shift already saved entries to another day. The selected time zone affects how dates and new daily boundaries are interpreted."},{"id":"completion-rate","category":"statistics","question":"How is completion rate calculated?","aliases":["How do you calculate my completion percentage?","Why is my completion rate lower than expected?","What is the denominator for completion rate?"],"keywords":["percentage","consistency","scheduled opportunities","qualifying entries","denominator","analytics"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"For an active tracker with scheduled opportunities, the consistency percentage is the number of qualifying opportunities divided by the number of counted opportunities, rounded to a whole percent. Standard Mode counts scheduled dates except holidays; Strict Mode counts every active date, including otherwise unscheduled dates and holidays. The current as-of date is left out when it has no entry yet. If there are no counted opportunities, the percentage is unavailable."},{"id":"qualifying-checkin","category":"statistics","question":"What makes a check-in count as successful?","aliases":["What counts as a completed day?","Why did my check-in not count toward progress?"],"keywords":["success rule","threshold","qualifying","recorded","outcome","measure"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/types.ts"],"answer":"A recorded check-in qualifies when its outcome and values meet the tracker’s configured success rules. A tracker can have multiple measures and rules, so recording something does not always mean the day qualifies. A skipped check-in is not a qualifying recorded result."},{"id":"points-and-rewards","category":"statistics","question":"How do achievement points and streak rewards work?","aliases":["Do I lose reward points if my streak resets?","What earns points in Achievements?"],"keywords":["achievements","points","reward","qualified check-in","milestone","longest streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progressionModel.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/services/supabase/progressionRepository.ts","src/features/dashboard/AchievementsPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/ProgressionAchievementsPage.tsx","src/features/dashboard/achievementCatalog.ts","src/features/dashboard/BadgeCelebrationDialog.tsx","src/features/dashboard/ProgressionAchievementsPage.test.tsx","src/features/dashboard/BadgeCelebrationDialog.test.tsx","supabase/tests/progression_achievements.test.sql","src/features/dashboard/LegacyAchievementsPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/schemaVersionGate.ts","supabase/migrations/20261104002200_preserve_deleted_tracker_reward_context.sql","supabase/migrations/20261104002300_add_perfect_month_and_comeback_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000200_make_dedicated_one_time.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000300_repeatable_activity_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000700_require_full_consistency_window.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000800_publish_consistency_qualification_details.sql"],"answer":"The legacy Achievements view calculates its points from local saved history. When a build enables progression, Wins shows server-confirmed XP, level, reward history, and 14 achievement badges. A qualifying check-in earns 10 XP, a Perfect Day earns 20 XP, streak milestones at 7, 14, 30, and 100 qualifying opportunities earn 35, 50, 100, and 200 XP, a goal milestone earns 25 XP, and a completed goal earns 100 XP. Badges themselves add no XP. The confirmed XP total comes from the server ledger; offline check-in estimates are provisional until synchronization confirms them. Level thresholds are 0, 100, 300, and 600 XP for levels 1 through 4, with each next level requiring 100 times the current level number in additional XP. Existing accounts may show one balance snapshot labeled “XP reconstructed from past activity”; it is not an itemized reward history and does not unlock achievements.\n\nFirst Step, the streak badges, Consistency Star, and Dedicated are one-time badges. Dedicated’s migration preserves its existing award and reversal history. Perfect Day repeats once per distinct qualifying date; Perfect Week repeats for a distinct completed qualifying week; Perfect Month repeats for a distinct completed qualifying month; The Comeback repeats for a distinct qualifying recovery episode; Milestone Maker repeats for each distinct configured goal milestone; and Goal Crusher repeats for each distinct confirmed goal completion. These awards use server-confirmed reward identities, so retries do not duplicate an occurrence and pre-cutover history is not retroactively awarded. When a source reward is reversed, its linked badge occurrence is revoked while both events remain in history; a later qualifying generation can earn it again.\n\nConsistency Star requires both at least 30 completed eligible opportunities and at least 80% adherence. Standard Mode treats holidays and unscheduled rest days as neutral; Strict Mode counts active-period dates as opportunities. Wins shows the server-computed eligible-day coverage and adherence separately, and does not infer either value from a client-side approximation. The server also supplies current incomplete Perfect Week progress toward three qualifying dates and Perfect Month progress toward 12 qualifying dates when schedule history is supported. It reports failed or unavailable periods explicitly. Comeback progress is descriptive rather than a percentage because qualification depends on a genuine missed required opportunity followed by seven consecutive qualifying opportunities on that tracker; neutral dates preserve the run and a saved skip does not start it.\n\nA newly confirmed badge occurrence can trigger one celebration, presented in sequence. The first occurrence receives a grand celebration; ordinary repeats are subtle; award counts 5, 10, 25, 50, and each additional 100 receive a grand milestone celebration. Existing history is marked seen on initial account load and is not replayed. Acknowledgement is saved when the dialog is dismissed, and the event identity suppresses duplicate presentations across retries and navigation. Permanent deletion offers Keep My Wins, which preserves eligible rewards and their history, or Delete Tracker and Wins, which removes only rewards linked to that tracker. If rewards cannot be safely separated, deletion stops. The progression view stays disabled unless the build sets `VITE_ENABLE_PROGRESSION_UI=true`."},{"id":"repeatable-progress-badges","category":"statistics","question":"What do Perfect Month and The Comeback badges require?","aliases":["How do I earn Perfect Month?","How do I earn The Comeback badge?"],"keywords":["Perfect Month","The Comeback","achievement","holiday","streak","badge"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progressionModel.ts","src/features/dashboard/achievementCatalog.ts","supabase/migrations/20261104002300_add_perfect_month_and_comeback_achievements.sql","supabase/migrations/20261105000300_repeatable_activity_achievements.sql"],"answer":"Perfect Month is earned after a completed month when every required opportunity qualifies, across at least 12 distinct dates with required activity. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral; Strict Mode still requires qualifying activity on them. The Comeback is earned after a qualifying tracker opportunity is followed by a genuinely missed required opportunity, then seven consecutive qualifying eligible opportunities. A saved skip does not trigger recovery, and neutral dates preserve the recovery run. Both badges can be earned again for a different month or recovery episode. Wins shows current incomplete week and month progress when the server can verify the schedule history. Comeback eligibility is shown as a description because it depends on several linked conditions. These badges add no XP, and unsupported history is not reconstructed."},{"id":"completion-missed-dates","category":"statistics","question":"Do missed dates affect completion rate?","aliases":["Does a missed day lower my consistency percentage?","Why did my completion rate decrease after an unchecked day?"],"keywords":["completion rate","missed opportunity","denominator","consistency"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"Counted opportunities contribute to the denominator, while qualifying entries contribute to the numerator. A missed counted opportunity therefore lowers the percentage. Standard Mode excludes holidays and unscheduled days; Strict Mode counts every active date."},{"id":"completion-holidays-rest-days","category":"statistics","question":"Do holidays and rest days affect completion rate?","aliases":["Are holidays included in consistency statistics?","Do unscheduled dates count in the percentage?"],"keywords":["completion rate","holidays","rest days","Standard Mode","Strict Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, holidays and unscheduled rest days are excluded from counted opportunities. Strict Mode counts every active date, including holidays and dates outside the regular schedule. A saved qualifying check-in on a holiday can count in either mode."},{"id":"completion-no-opportunities","category":"statistics","question":"Why is a tracker’s completion rate unavailable?","aliases":["Why is there no percentage for this tracker?","What if my tracker has no counted dates yet?"],"keywords":["completion rate","no opportunities","active period","schedule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"The percentage is unavailable when there are no counted opportunities in the selected period. This can happen before a tracker’s active period or when its schedule and mode produce no opportunities in that range."},{"id":"analytics-metric-units","category":"statistics","question":"Does Analytics combine different measure units into one total?","aliases":["Are pages and minutes added together in Analytics?","How does Insights summarize multiple kinds of values?"],"keywords":["Analytics","Insights","measures","units","observations"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/analytics/AnalyticsPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. Analytics summarizes each measure separately, so values with different units are not added together. Comparable counts such as completed opportunities can be combined, while measure values stay with their own tracker and unit."},{"id":"completion-holiday-entry","category":"statistics","question":"Does a check-in on a holiday count toward completion rate?","aliases":["If I log on a holiday, does my percentage go up?","Does holiday progress count in consistency statistics?"],"keywords":["completion rate","holiday","qualifying check-in","Strict Mode","Standard Mode"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.test.ts"],"answer":"It depends on the tracker’s mode. Standard Mode excludes holidays from counted opportunities, so a holiday entry does not affect that rate. Strict Mode counts every active date, including holidays, and a qualifying saved entry contributes to the rate."},{"id":"standard-vs-strict","category":"streaks","question":"What is the difference between Standard Mode and Strict Mode?","aliases":["Does Strict Mode count rest days?","Which days become opportunities in Strict Mode?"],"keywords":["Standard Mode","Strict Mode","schedule","daily","opportunity","holidays"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx"],"answer":"Standard Mode counts the tracker’s scheduled dates as opportunities and pauses over unscheduled days and holidays. Strict Mode counts every date in the active period, including unscheduled dates and holidays. A saved qualifying check-in on a holiday can still count in either mode."},{"id":"streak-statistics","category":"streaks","question":"How do streak statistics work?","aliases":["How are streaks calculated?","What counts toward my current streak?","Why did my streak reset?"],"keywords":["current streak","longest streak","qualifying check-in","schedule","strict mode","rest day","holiday"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Your current streak is the run of recent tracking opportunities you have met. Your longest streak is the best qualifying run in the tracker’s history. A missed required opportunity can end the current run, while the longest record remains. Which dates count depends on the tracker’s schedule, Strict Mode, and holidays."},{"id":"all-trackers-streak","category":"streaks","question":"How does the All Trackers streak work?","aliases":["Is the All Trackers streak the sum of my tracker streaks?","What is an account-wide Perfect Day streak?"],"keywords":["All Trackers","account streak","Perfect Day","shared streak"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/features/dashboard/DashboardPage.tsx","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"It counts consecutive dates when at least one tracker has a required opportunity and every required tracker qualifies. It is separate from each tracker’s own streak. Standard Mode holidays and rest days are neutral; Strict Mode requires active-period dates. A known failed opportunity ends the run, while a neutral or still-pending date does not add a day or prematurely break the confirmed run."},{"id":"rest-days-streaks","category":"streaks","question":"How do rest days affect streaks?","aliases":["Do unscheduled days break a streak?","Does my schedule pause my streak?"],"keywords":["schedule","unscheduled","opportunity","strict mode","rest day"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.ts"],"answer":"In Standard Mode, only scheduled check-in dates are opportunities, so unscheduled rest days do not break a streak. Strict Mode treats every active date as an opportunity, including dates outside the regular schedule. Tracker start and deadline dates still bound the active period."},{"id":"streak-longest","category":"streaks","question":"What is the difference between my current streak and longest streak?","aliases":["Does losing my streak erase my record?","Why is my longest streak higher than my current streak?"],"keywords":["current streak","longest streak","record","history"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"Your current streak describes your ongoing qualifying run. Your longest streak is the best qualifying run found in the tracker’s history, so a current streak ending does not erase that record."},{"id":"streak-skipped","category":"streaks","question":"Does marking a check-in as skipped count toward a streak?","aliases":["Is an intentionally missed entry a completed day?","Does “Marked missed intentionally” qualify for a streak?"],"keywords":["skipped","marked missed","streak","qualifying entry"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"No. A Skipped entry is a saved intentional outcome, not a derived Missed date or a recorded No progress check-in. It does not qualify for a streak on a required opportunity. Standard Mode rest days and holidays are excluded from the streak; Strict Mode requires qualifying activity on every in-period date."},{"id":"streak-zero-quantity","category":"streaks","question":"Does recording zero keep a streak alive?","aliases":["Can a zero quantity value qualify for a streak?","Why did my zero entry not count toward my streak?"],"keywords":["zero","quantity","streak qualification","success rule"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/progression.ts","src/domain/trackers/progression.test.ts"],"answer":"A numeric zero does not qualify through the default streak rule, which requires a finite value greater than zero. A tracker with an explicit streak qualification uses that configured rule instead, so check its settings when the result is unexpected."},{"id":"restore-deleted-tracker","category":"trackers","question":"Can I restore a deleted tracker?","aliases":["Where do deleted trackers go?","How do I recover a tracker from the Bin?"],"keywords":["Bin","restore","deleted tracker","archive","recover"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Move a tracker to the Bin to keep its saved progress and plan. Choose Restore to use it again. If a restore is still in progress, the tracker stays unavailable until it finishes. Archiving is different: an archived tracker stays in your library with its history."},{"id":"bin-retention","category":"trackers","question":"What happens to a tracker after I delete it?","aliases":["Is a deleted tracker erased immediately?","How long can I restore something from The Bin?"],"keywords":["Move to Bin","Bin","Restore","Permanently Delete","Keep My Wins","Delete Tracker and Wins"],"suggestible":false,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx","src/db/localRepository.ts"],"answer":"Moving a tracker to the Bin keeps its saved progress and rewards. You can restore it while it is in the Bin. Permanently Delete cannot be undone. Choose Keep My Wins to remove the tracker and its activity while preserving earned XP, badges, achievements, reward history, and appropriate tracker context. Choose Delete Tracker and Wins to remove the tracker and its activity and reverse only rewards linked to it. Other rewards and achievements stay. If rewards cannot be safely separated, nothing is deleted; choose Keep My Wins instead."},{"id":"edit-tracker-history","category":"trackers","question":"Do tracker edits change historical statistics?","aliases":["What happens to old stats when I edit a tracker?","Can changing a measure change old entries?"],"keywords":["edit","historical","measure type","schedule","statistics"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/invariants.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/analytics.ts"],"answer":"Some edits can change which dates count in schedule-based statistics, because calculations use the tracker’s current schedule and active period. A saved measure’s type and historical interpretation are protected. Retiring a measure removes it from future check-ins while retaining its definition for old entries."},{"id":"archive-tracker","category":"trackers","question":"What happens when I archive a tracker?","aliases":["Does archiving delete my tracker history?","Can I restore a paused tracker?"],"keywords":["archive","pause","active","history","delete"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerBinPage.tsx"],"answer":"Archiving a tracker removes it from Today and current activity while keeping its recorded history and rewards. The tracker list can show active, archived, or all trackers. When editing an archived tracker, choose whether to keep it archived or move it to active after saving. Deleting a tracker is a separate action that moves it through the app’s Bin and restore flow."},{"id":"tracker-schedules","category":"trackers","question":"How do tracker schedules work?","aliases":["Which days count as scheduled?","How do I choose tracking days?"],"keywords":["schedule","weekly","daily","weekdays","opportunity"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx"],"answer":"The schedule defines the regular days when a tracker has a check-in opportunity. You choose it while creating or editing a tracker. Standard Mode uses those scheduled dates for streak and consistency opportunities; Strict Mode treats every active date as an opportunity."},{"id":"start-date-deadline","category":"trackers","question":"How do a tracker’s start date and deadline affect it?","aliases":["When does a tracker begin counting?","Does a deadline stop future check-ins?"],"keywords":["start date","deadline","active period","schedule","tracker"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/activePeriod.test.ts","src/domain/trackers/planning.test.ts","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx"],"answer":"The tracker’s active period is bounded by its start date and, when set, its deadline. Dates outside that period are not active tracking opportunities. A deadline therefore stops schedule-based calculations from counting later dates."},{"id":"retire-measure","category":"trackers","question":"What happens when I retire a measure?","aliases":["Can I remove a measure but keep its history?","Why is an old measure still shown in History?"],"keywords":["retire","measure","old entries","history","future check-ins"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/domain/trackers/types.ts","src/domain/trackers/schema.test.ts","src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Retiring a measure removes it from future check-ins while keeping its definition available to interpret older entries. That is why an old measure may still appear when you review historical data."},{"id":"tracker-editing","category":"trackers","question":"How do I edit a tracker?","aliases":["Where can I change a tracker’s schedule?","Can I add another measure to a tracker?"],"keywords":["edit","tracker","schedule","measures","configuration"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerConfigurationEditor.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerSetupPage.test.tsx"],"answer":"Open Trackers, choose the tracker’s edit action, update its supported settings, then save. You can change configuration such as its schedule and add measures, while saved measure types and their historical meaning are protected."},{"id":"tracker-created-active-date","category":"trackers","question":"Does a tracker count dates before I created it?","aliases":["Does its start date include days before the tracker existed?","Why does a tracker created today start counting today?"],"keywords":["tracker creation date","start date","active period","workspace time zone"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/domain/trackers/planning.ts","src/domain/trackers/activePeriod.test.ts"],"answer":"No. The effective active period starts on the later of the configured start date and the tracker’s creation date in the workspace time zone. Earlier dates are outside the tracker’s active period."},{"id":"archived-checkin-history","category":"trackers","question":"Can I edit check-ins after archiving a tracker?","aliases":["Is archived tracker history read-only?","Does archiving keep old entries but stop edits?"],"keywords":["archived tracker","check-in","history","read-only","archive"],"suggestible":true,"sources":["src/features/history/HistoryPage.tsx","src/features/trackers/TrackerLibraryPage.tsx"],"answer":"Archiving keeps the tracker’s saved history, but its check-ins are read-only while the tracker is archived. Restore it to active status if you need to edit its check-ins again."}] as const
